const CCW_TEARDOWNS={"cbs23": {"title": "Teardown: 1st place, CBS 2023 Vestas", "facts": ["Opens on one slide with Vision, Question, Solution and Impact before any analysis.", "Impact is quantified up front: 13% EBIT margin and 20% ROCE by 2030, and 12% of EU green hydrogen production supported.", "Insights section uses a market chart (global green hydrogen revenue 2022 vs 2030, CAGR 39.5%) and ties it to Vestas's core competencies.", "Maps the Power-to-X value chain in six stages and marks where Vestas has capability and where it does not, which makes 'where to play' an evidence-based choice.", "Cites sources on slides (for example GWEC, IEA).", "A section tracker at the foot of each slide (Insights, Ideas, Implementation, Impact) keeps the judges oriented in a 59-page file that includes appendix material.", "Viewed slides 2 and 4 as images: clean one-message slides with action titles and a source line."], "lessons": ["State the answer and the numbers on slide 2.", "Choose where to play from a capability gap table, not a feeling.", "Source every market number."], "source": "https://usercontent.one/wp/www.casecompetition.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/The-University-of-Hong-Kong-2.pdf"}, "pcc21": {"title": "Teardown: winner, Polit Impact 2021 (BMS and Vixtocar)", "facts": ["Opens with Situation, Question, Strategy, Impact and a headline claim: introduce the treatment as standard care and reach 5.6 bn DKK revenue by 2033.", "Maps the three parties (the company, the national medical council, patients) and finds the common ground: reducing uncertainty about effectiveness.", "Models three extrapolation scenarios (bull, base, bear) with QALY and ICER and compares each to the willingness-to-pay line; only the bear case is above it.", "Recommends a performance-based pricing model that starts with a discount and rises as long-term effectiveness is proven.", "Slide titles are full-sentence claims, with a section tracker (Complication, Apprehension, Reaction, Timeline).", "Imperfections to learn from: on slide 8 the base-case saving per QALY reads -6,000 although the table beside it (546,000 vs 652,000) implies -106,000, which matches slide 5; the chart on slide 5 has overlapping labels; and the sentence 'all scenarios except the bear case will be above the WTP line' is ambiguous. The product and the figures belong to the case pack, not a real company outcome."], "lessons": ["Find the point where all stakeholders agree and design the solution around it.", "Show bull, base and bear, and be honest that the bear case fails.", "Titles that carry the argument."], "source": "https://www.politcasecompetition.com/s/IMPACT2021Winner.pdf"}};
const CCW_LAB={"title": "Case pack lab", "steps": ["Pick a case pack from the gallery and read the task and judging criteria first (20 min).", "Set a timer (90 minutes for a quick pass, 24 hours for the full simulation) and attempt it without opening any winner deck.", "Write your own one-page executive summary: key question, situation, solution, impact, the numbers you would defend.", "Open the winning deck and compare only its executive summary against yours.", "Score both on the NIBS rubric (issue 10, analysis 20, recommendation 20, implementation 20, creativity 10, presentation 10, Q&A 10).", "Read the rest of the winner and list three things it did that you did not, and one weakness you can see.", "Save your notes and redo the weakest section."], "checklist": ["Does the first content slide state the answer?", "Are impact numbers quantified and labelled as estimates?", "Is each slide title a claim?", "Is there a visible risk and mitigation?", "Is every market number sourced?", "Where does the deck contain a numeric inconsistency or an ambiguous statement?"], "note": "Numbers in winning decks are team projections on case-pack data, not company results."};
